    "narrative": "The Austin Waves face a favorable slate today, highlighted by **Kyle Tucker** (75.38) and **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** (74.56) as our strongest plays. **Kyle Tucker** earns the top spot through a combination of high base projection and a soft matchup against Nick Martinez, while **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** benefits immensely from the high-upside pairing of the favorable Spence matchup and a premium #2 spot in the order. Both players anchor our core, leveraging the projected 6.03 xERA of Spence to push the offensive ceiling. **Andy Pages** (69.52) also registers as a strong start, maintaining high efficiency despite his aggressive baserunning profile, which actually carries a slight weight penalty here given the matchup volatility.\n\nThe most difficult decision on the bench involved **Cole Carrigg** (58.50) and **Wade Meckler** (58.29). While both are technically starts, **Cole Carrigg** narrowly edged out **Wade Meckler** for a spot in the primary rotation due to a favorable wind factor and the switch-hitting versatility that mitigates the threat of Shota Imanaga. We are keeping a close eye on the \"Lineup Pending\" status for **Jacob Wilson**, **Andy Pages**, **Wade Meckler**, **Kyle Tucker**, and **Nolan Schanuel**; any significant drop in batting order for these players could force a late-inning recalibration of our efficiency targets.\n\nWe continue to operate without the services of **Luis Robert Jr.** and **Jordan Westburg** due to injury, while **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** and **Gunnar Henderson** are unavailable today due to schedule gaps. **Liam Hicks** (45.31) remains a marginal start; while he holds the leadoff spot, his matchup against Wheeler represents our highest SP_xERA risk of the day. We are banking on his volume as the #1 hitter to sustain value, but his score sits perilously close to our sub-40 floor, making him the most likely candidate to be swapped should official lineups reveal a pinch-hitting risk or defensive substitution trend.",
